  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAFEGUARDING THE ANCESTRAL RAINFORESTS LANDSCAPE OF NORTHWESTERN GUATEMALA BY STRENGTHENING MAYAN CONSERVATION LEADERSHIP FOR HABITAT PROTECTION AND SUSTAINABLE ALTERNATIVE LIVELIHOODS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO STRENGTHEN THE LONG-TERM CONSERVATION OF THE ANCESTRAL RAINFORESTS LANDSCAPE IN THE GUATEMALAN MAYA FOREST AND ITS RICH BIODIVERSITY BY SUPPORTING MAYAN CONSERVATION LEADERSHIP, PROMOTING SUSTAINABLE ALTERNATIVE LIVELIHOODS, AND ENHANCING CLIMATE RESILIENCE. THIS WORK SEEKS TO EMPOWER INDIGENOUS LAND STEWARDSHIP TO REDUCE THE RISKS OF MEGAPROJECTS, MONOCULTURE EXPANSION, AND CLIMATE CHANGE. SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: 1) CULTURALLY RELEVANT CONSULTATIONS, CONSENSUS-BUILDING PROCESSES AND HANDS-ON TRAINING TO EMPOWER 20 OUTSTANDING LOCAL LEADERS AND AUTHORITIES TO IDENTIFY THEIR OWN CONSERVATION AND SUSTAINABLE LIVELIHOOD SOLUTIONS 2) IMPLEMENT COMMUNITY-LED INITIATIVES THAT PROMOTE HABITAT AND BIODIVERSITY CONSERVATION AND SUSTAINABLE ALTERNATIVE LIVELIHOODS IN THREE STRATEGIC SITES OF THE LANDSCAPE AND 3) EDUCATE AND SHARE LESSONS LEARNED WITH 50 ADDITIONAL INDIGENOUS COMMUNITIES USING MEDIA CAMPAIGNS THAT ENCOURAGE MINDFUL NATURAL RESOURCE MANAGEMENT, SUSTAINABLE LIVELIHOODS, AND CLIMATE ADAPTATION.</narrative>
  </description>
